From 7a3718c91aebab02adcfeaa062a0eac02a01b78a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:45:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 096/109] test: cover image classification on executorch and
 onnxruntime

test_classifier_layout checks the et and ort graph names for the text,
image, none, label-mismatch and labels-confinement cases, both through the
shared detector and through each recipe's checkpoint resolver, and that
both recipes accept the image-classification label.

server_image_classify.py takes --wrapped-server tflite|executorch|onnxruntime
and runs the whole suite for that recipe, with per-engine graph, model names
and *_args. A new test checks that a label/layout mismatch fails the load
with both layouts named. The fake engine takes --engine et-server|ort-server
and then reports no task on /health, as those engines do.

test_514's 12 MiB upload is synthetic, so a real engine's decoder refuses
it; against a real engine the test now expects that 400, which still shows
the body passed lemond's cap.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
